\begin_layout Chapter
The Perspectives of Bio7
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In the perspective bar several different perspectives can be activated via the perspective buttons.
 All the views or editors in the perspective can be closed,
 opened,
 detached or moved.
 The perspectives in Bio7 can be extended with several other views which can be opened in the 
\series bold
\noun on
Windows\SpecialChar menuseparator
Views
\series default
\noun default
 menu or with the default action in the status bar at the bottom left of the program.
 Additionally self defined perspectives can be created or deleted.
 From the Eclipse Workbench User Guide (
\begin_inset Flex URL
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
http://help.eclipse.org
\end_layout

\end_inset

):
 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

Perspectives provide combinations of views and editors that are suited to performing a particular set of tasks....
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
\begin_inset VSpace medskip
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph*
To open a new perspective:
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Click the 
\series bold
Open Perspective
\series default
 button on the shortcut bar on the left side of the Workbench window.
 (This provides the same function as the 
\series bold
\noun on
Window \SpecialChar menuseparator
 Open Perspective
\series default
\noun default
 menu on the menu bar.) 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
To see a complete list of perspectives,
 select 
\series bold
Other...

\series default
 from the drop-down menu.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Select the perspective that you want to open.
 When the perspective opens,
 the title bar of the window changes to display the name of the perspective.
 In addition,
 an icon is added to the shortcut bar,
 allowing you to quickly switch back to that perspective from other perspectives in the same window.
 
\end_layout

