\begin_layout Paragraph
Transfer Selected Data To R
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
IJ RT:
\series default
 Transfers the values of an opened ImageJ Results Table to R as a dataframe.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
IJ RasterStack:
\series default
 Transfers an opened ImageJ stack as a list of matrices or (with the option Raster?) as a RasterStack to R. The data type is selected in the combo box below Pic<-.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
ROI:
\series default
 Transfers the x, y coordinates of the current selection (ROI) to R.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Particles:
\series default
 Opens the Analyze Particles dialog of ImageJ, the results of the particle analysis are transferred to R as a dataframe.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Pixel:
\series default
 Transfers the selected pixels (freehand, rectangle, etc.) of one or several images with or without a signature as a matrix to R.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Selection RM:
\series default
 Transfers the coordinates of the selections of the ROI Manager as a list of lists to R (see the Geometry Selections view for spatial data).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Pixel RM:
\series default
 Transfers the pixels of the selections of the ROI Manager (all images) with or without a signature as a matrix to R.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Pixel RM Stack:
\series default
 Transfers the pixels of the selections of the ROI Manager for all slices of a stack with or without a signature as a matrix to R.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
Transfer Image Data From and To R
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Pic<-:
\series default
 Transfers the image data of the active image to R with the name of the text field below and the data type of the combo box (
\series bold
Double
\series default
, 
\series bold
Integer
\series default
, 
\series bold
Byte
\series default
 or 
\series bold
RGB Byte
\series default
).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Pic->:
\series default
 Creates an image from an R matrix or vector (the name of the R object in the text field below) with the image type of the combo box (
\series bold
Colour
\series default
, 
\series bold
Greyscale
\series default
, 
\series bold
Float
\series default
, 
\series bold
Short
\series default
 or 
\series bold
Double
\series default
). The type Double creates a 64-bit double image of SWTImageJ (the values of R without a conversion to float).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
Multivariate Image Analysis
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Cluster Pic:
\series default
 Performs a cluster analysis (clara or kmeans) and creates a new image from the assigned pixels.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
PCA:
\series default
 Performs a principal component analysis and creates new images from the components.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection
Image Transfer to R
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
With 
\series bold
Pic<-
\series default
 and 
\series bold
Pic->
\series default
 the data of the active image are transferred to R or image data from R to ImageJ in a selected data type (image type). It is good practice to transfer the image data in the smallest data type needed for a task. In addition special transfers are available for selected image data:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Pixel
\series default
 transfers the data of the current selection (one selection) of one or several images (opened tabs or views) in the selected data type without the ROI Manager.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Pixel RM
\series default
 transfers the pixels of the selections of the ROI Manager (the selected selections or all selections if none is selected) for all opened images with a selected or an incremental signature. If a stack is among the opened images only the first slice is transferred.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Pixel RM Stack
\series default
 transfers the pixels of the selections of the ROI Manager for all slices of a stack (e.g., multispectral or hyperspectral image data) with a selected or an incremental signature.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Note that image folders can be dropped on the ImageJ-Canvas view to load the images as a regular or virtual stack (in a virtual stack only the displayed image is loaded into the memory). A description of the ROI Manager can be found in the ImageJ user guide.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection
Supervised Classification with ImageJ and R
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The custom class signatures of 
\series bold
Pixel RM
\series default
 and 
\series bold
Pixel RM Stack
\series default
 are especially useful for a supervised classification of image data in R: every selection could represent a vegetation or a tissue type (e.g., a plant species or a tumor) with several spectral bands (the slices of a stack) for the training of a classifier. See the Bio7 examples (https://github.com/Bio7/Bio7) and the Bio7 classification plugin (https://github.com/Bio7/Bio7_Classification).
\end_layout

