\begin_layout Section
The 3d Perspective
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "sec:The-3d-Perspective"

\end_inset

\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The 3d perspective of Bio7 visualizes data, models and simulations in an OpenGL view (Jogl). It combines several tools in one 3D view: an interactive 
\series bold
plot API
\series default
 for 3D plots and charts (surfaces, scatter plots, bars, box plots, pie charts, etc.) with an export to an interactive web page (WebGL) or to Blender, the display of 
\series bold
height maps
\series default
 from ImageJ images, the 
\series bold
volume rendering
\series default
 and 
\series bold
iso surfaces
\series default
 of ImageJ stacks with clipping, cuts and 3D 
\series bold
measurements
\series default
, the import of 
\series bold
3D models
\series default
 (*.obj, *.stl, *.ply, *.off) and custom 
\series bold
OpenGL code
\series default
 (Java) for models and simulations. In addition interactive 
\series bold
HTML simulations
\series default
 can be exported which run in a web browser.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The 3d perspective can be opened in the perspective bar of Bio7 (3d). By default it contains the 
\series bold
Space
\series default
 view (the 3D view), the 
\series bold
Options Space
\series default
 view with the settings of the 3D view, the Console and the Project Explorer.
\end_layout

