\begin_layout Subsection
HTML Simulations
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "subsec:HTML-Simulations"

\end_inset

\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The class 
\family typewriter
HtmlSimulation
\family default
 exports an interactive simulation to a single HTML page (without dependencies, WebGL for 3D). The simulation runs in the web browser: the model is written in JavaScript with the functions 
\family typewriter
setup(sim)
\family default
 (called at the start and with Reset) and 
\family typewriter
step(sim)
\family default
 (one time step). The page contains Play/Pause, Step, Reset, the speed, the controls of the settings (sliders, number fields, text fields, check boxes, choices and buttons) and an optional chart of values over time. The settings are available in the model as 
\family typewriter
sim.p.name
\family default
.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The view of a simulation is a 2D grid (
\family typewriter
View.GRID_2D
\family default
, e.g., a cellular automaton with optional agents), a 3D scene (
\family typewriter
View.SCENE_3D
\family default
, points and lines, e.g., a swarm) or a dynamic surface (
\family typewriter
View.SURFACE_3D
\family default
, e.g., a diffusion).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Float table
placement H
alignment document
wide false
sideways false
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "basicstyle={\rmfamily},language=Java,numbers=left"
inline false
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
new HtmlSimulation("Game of Life")
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
    .view(HtmlSimulation.View.GRID_2D)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
    .number("size", "Grid size (cells)", 120)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
    .slider("density", "Start density", 0, 1, 0.01, 0.3)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
    .restartOn("size", "density")
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
    .chart("Population")
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
    .scriptFile("/path/GameOfLife.js") // the model in a JavaScript file
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
    .export("/path/GameOfLife.html");
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
\begin_inset Caption Standard

\begin_layout Plain Layout
An HTML simulation with the model in a JavaScript file
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The model can be embedded as a string (
\family typewriter
code
\family default
) or loaded from a JavaScript file (
\family typewriter
scriptFile
\family default
) which can be edited in an editor of Bio7 (e.g., the generic editor). The export copies the script file next to the page or merges it into one HTML file (
\family typewriter
embedScript(true)
\family default
). A template of a script file is created with 
\family typewriter
HtmlSimulation.writeScriptTemplate(file)
\family default
. Several examples are available in the folder html of the Bio7 Java examples (e.g., the Game of Life, an epidemic model, a forest fire, a swarm, a heat diffusion, a reaction-diffusion model and foraging ants).
\end_layout

