\begin_layout Subsection
Fullscreen Mode
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The Space view can be displayed in the fullscreen mode with the keys F2 (the primary monitor), F3 (the secondary monitor), F4 (the tertiary monitor) and F5 (a selected monitor). The fullscreen mode is quit with the Escape key (or F2). The switch to the fullscreen mode creates a new OpenGL context and invokes the setup method again, so textures, TextRenderer objects and models of custom code should be created in the setup method.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
The WorldWind Perspective
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "sec:The-WorldWind-Perspective"

\end_inset

\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The WorldWind perspective can be opened in the perspective bar (WorldWind). It embeds the 
\series bold
WorldWind
\series default
 view with the virtual globe of NASA WorldWind Java (https://worldwind.arc.nasa.gov/java/) and the 
\series bold
Options WorldWind
\series default
 view with the settings of the globe in several tabs (Control, Default Layers, Layers, Render, Measure and Projection). The globe displays satellite images, maps, elevations, boundaries and place names and in addition own data: ImageJ images, GeoTIFF images, shapefiles and custom OpenGL layers (Java).
\end_layout

