\begin_layout Standard
With the Layers tab own data can be displayed on the globe: GeoTIFF images (
\series bold
Add GeoTIFF
\series default
), shapefiles (
\series bold
Add Shapefile
\series default
), the active ImageJ image as a static layer (
\series bold
IJ image
\series default
) or as a dynamic layer which is updated with the image (
\series bold
IJ Dynamic
\series default
, e.g., an animated stack) and a custom OpenGL layer of compiled Java code (
\series bold
Dyn. Layer
\series default
). An added layer gets its own panel with the controls of the layer (e.g., the opacity and the removal of the layer).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The 
\series bold
Latitude
\series default
 and 
\series bold
Longitude
\series default
 fields define the area of an image on the globe (the minimum and maximum), 
\series bold
Go to
\series default
 flies to the area. 
\series bold
Get Area
\series default
 fills the fields with the values of special variables in R (e.g., an area which is georeferenced in R), with 
\series bold
Compute
\series default
 the corners of an area can be picked on the globe (alternately the minimum and the maximum, disable the toggle after the selection). 
\series bold
Image Alpha
\series default
 makes a color of an image transparent. So, e.g., an R plot (ImageJ is the default plot device of R in Bio7) can be positioned on the globe.
\end_layout

