\begin_layout Section
The R Perspective and Menus
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "sec:The-R-Perspective"

\end_inset

\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Bio7 embeds R for the statistical analysis of data, images and models. R is connected with 
\series bold
Rserve
\series default
: 
\series bold
R > Start Rserve
\series default
 starts R in the Bio7 console and the Rserve server in this R session (cooperative mode on Linux and macOS), then Bio7 connects to the server (displayed in the progress dialog and in the console). After the connection has been established R can be used in the R-Shell view, the R editor, the Table view, the ImageJ views and with the scripts and the compiler of Bio7. The path to R, the R startup arguments, the Rserve startup arguments (e.g., a port) and the client port are set in the R preferences (see 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "subsec:Rserve-preferences"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"
nolink "false"

\end_inset

).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
R Menus in the Bio7 Main Menu
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "subsec:R-Menus-in"

\end_inset

\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Start Rserve:
\series default
 Starts R with an Rserve connection (or stops the connection).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Load Workspace, Save Workspace:
\series default
 Loads or saves an R workspace (*.RData).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Evaluate Expression:
\series default
 Opens a dialog to evaluate an R expression, the result is displayed in the console.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Evaluate Line or Selection:
\series default
 Evaluates the selected text or the current line of the R editor and moves to the next line. A line is only evaluated if the expression is complete, else it is collected until the expression is complete (interrupt with the action of the R-Shell view).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Evaluate Clipboard:
\series default
 Evaluates the R script in the clipboard.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Get Clipboard Data:
\series default
 Transfers the data of the clipboard (e.g., cells of a spreadsheet) to the R workspace as the dataframe clip.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Remove All Objects:
\series default
 Removes all objects of the current workspace.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Start RGui with Workspace:
\series default
 Windows: starts RGui with the current workspace.
\end_layout

