 If something went wrong with the installation it can make sense to start Rserve in a OS shell to get more information about the installation process (see 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "subsec:Rserve-preferences"
nolink "false"

\end_inset

).
 To find the right R package some search facilities are available to find the package in the package list and to get some information about the package (select the 
\series bold
Open Package Description
\series default
 option).
 With the
\series bold
 Update Installed Packages
\series default
 action all currently installed R packages (except the Rserve package) will be updated if possible.
 
