\begin_layout Plain Layout
\begin_inset Caption Standard

\begin_layout Plain Layout
The R editor with errors and warnings.
 Error and warning quick fixes are indicated with a light bulb icon.
 Quick fixes can be opened (and applied) when hovering over the underlined error or warning.
 
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
\begin_inset VSpace medskip
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection
The Database View
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The database view contains three tabs to configure a database connection.
 For a database connection the ODBC drivers have to be installed for the dedicated Operating System.
 The R packages 
\series bold
odbc
\series default
 and 
\series bold
DBI
\series default
 have to be installed,
 too.
 In the first tab 
\series bold
Connection
\series default
 some templates are available which can be selected to be used for a custom connection and displays the connection information of the 
\series bold
Database
\series default
 and 
\series bold
SSH Tunnel
\series default
 tab.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
\begin_inset VSpace medskip
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
To start with a custom connection:
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Install the ODBC drivers and R packages (
\series bold
odbc
\series default
,
 
\series bold
DBI
\series default
)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Select one available default profile
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Update the login data on the 
\series bold
Database
\series default
 and (if enabled) 
\series bold
SSH Tunnel
\series default
 tab.
 In additon customize the 
\series bold
Custom Disconnect Code
\series default
 for a live connection.
 Please note if no database password should be stored for the database connection leave the password field blank.
 For each live database connection a password dialog will be opened to ask for the username and password (handy if you don't want to store the database password or the password should be hidden in a public area)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Store the current profile with the 
\series bold
Add Connection Profile
\series default
 action
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Use the 
\series bold
Connect
\series default
 action to establish a database connection
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Use the 
\series bold
Disconnect
\series default
 action to execute the R code given in the 
\series bold
Custom Disconnect Code
\series default
 textfield
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In the following section the different tabs and settings are described in detail.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
\begin_inset VSpace medskip
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
The Connection Tab Settings
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
The 
\series bold
Add Connection Profile
\series default
 action stores the current settings of the Database and SSH (if enabled) entries in a new profile and adds the selected name to the list of available 
\series bold
Stored Profiles
\series default
 (saved as a XML file in Bio7).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
The 
\series bold
Delete Stored Profile
\series default
 action deletes the current selected profile and removes the profile from the 
\series bold
Stored Profiles
\series default
 list.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
The 
\series bold
Use SSH Tunnel
\series default
 option adds the settings of the SSH Tunnel tab to the database tab settings which will be previewed in the 
\series bold
Preview
\series default
 textfield.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
The 
\series bold
Preview
\series default
 textfield shows the current settings of the database and SSH connection which can be stored as a database profile.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
The 
\series bold
Insert in Editor
\series default
 action transfers the database connection code to the current opened editor.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
The 
\series bold
Connect
\series default
 action establish a connection with the credentials given from the Database and SSH Tunnel tab.
 The connection is stored in the variable 
\series bold
con
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
The 
\series bold
Disconnect
\series default
 action executes R code given in the textfield 
\series bold
Custom Disconnect Code
\series default
 (available to control the SSH connection!)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
