\begin_layout Subsubsection
R Debugging Interface
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Since Bio7 2.0 a debugging GUI for R is integrated as part of the R editor.
 To debug a R script a breakpoint has to be set inside a R function.
 If a breakpoint is set several actions are added to the default Bio7 console.
 For the debugging process the native R console has to be started (The Rserve connection will be automatically change to the native mode if alive!).
 To start a debugging process the 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

Debug Trace Action
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 has to be invoked and the traced function has to be executed in the R shell (see screenshot below).
 In the shell several debugging actions are available:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
The 
\series bold
Debug Trace Action
\series default
 to start the debugging process.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
The 
\series bold
Stop
\series default
 action to stop the debugging process.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
The 
\series bold
Next
\series default
 action to go to the next statement.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
The 
\series bold
Continue
\series default
 action which continues with the execution without single stepping.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
The 
\series bold
Step Into
\series default
 action to step into function calls.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
The 
\series bold
Finish
\series default
 action to finish the current loop or function.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
A 
\series bold
Help
\series default
 action to display R debugging console commands.
\end_layout

